Z||000013||stimpy||08-04-2000||07:56 AM||||Yes, I did!  My set-up looks a lot like 1FST2M6's (now GT Bastards) set up. I don't have <B>quite</B> as fancy of components but the system definately rocks!  As far as Joe Salesguy quoting $200 for a custom enclosure in the footwell, I paid maybe $40 for materials for my fiberglass enclosure. The most expensive bits being the grill and the terminal cup. The fiberglass cost about $9 at Wally World and I still have enough cloth lft for several more.  It was the first time I did anything with fiberglass, and while its eay to mess up, it's also very easy to get right. Just Do It!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://gifs123.tripod.com/page15/renstimpy2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Philphine||08-04-2000||09:37 AM||||same basic method as stimpy. also no fiberglass expert, but the material is pretty cheap and once you do a few projects factory speaker locations won't limit you.<P>got wood and glass pods that hold 5 1/4 components in the dead pedal area a top dash center channel and a single rear speaker that is part of my 3rd brake light. the door 8's will be glassed in too. need to change to power windows first though.||||reg||1
Z||000015||1FST2M6||08-04-2000||01:42 PM||||i have the Sony head unit and the Xtant if anyone wants them... tried to sell them to GT Bastard but he just laughed... I have replacement warranty on the Xtant for the next 5 years, all recipts for every upgrade and the Xtant performace test at Xtant labs. upgraded boost/cut board (LFQ-45) have upgraded coil packs for better low frequency extension and to match the output of the 2000 model X2001 and 3 cases, one brushed stainless, one polished stainless, and one swirl brushed aluminum. the Sony is a dead head and must be accompanied by amps. I'm fighting with UPS on a package for GT Bastard trying to get him the sub that was last in that box.. according to UPS the magnet is hazardous caseu "it can cause other clients matiel to possibly fail" eg software and credit cards. and they want me to pay a $30 charge for handling.. A FREEKING SPEAKER! uum it showed up on my door step from you guys - WHATEVER! sorry UPS just bugs me somtimes..     <A HREF="http://www.xtant.com" TARGET=_blank>www.xtant.com</A>   <A HREF="http://www.sony.com" TARGET=_blank>www.sony.com</A>   <A HREF="http://www.xtant.com/products/1001x.cfm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.xtant.com/products/1001x.cfm</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 08-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||stimpy||08-04-2000||07:16 PM||||Almost afraid to ask... How much for the Xtant? There is a shop here inOKC that is "blowing them out" for $400 with no upgrades. That is a <B>serious</B> piece of equipment!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://gifs123.tripod.com/page15/renstimpy2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Black88GT||08-04-2000||11:19 PM||||I think the footwell sub is the best bet.  I talked to an audio guy and he said that if you put some sound dampening material under the dash and around the footwell sub it should make a difference.  I got my friend to make me a fiberglass box for a 10" sub.  12" subs get sloppy and hard to work with due to the large magnet.  I am using a Sony Xplode amp with that.  I have a crappy dash I am trying to cut and fit for 6 1/2" Infinity kappa components, if it works I will do it on a decent looking dash and paint it black to go in my fiero.  Eventually, I want 5 1/4" components in the doors, 4 inch components where the 4x6s go, and 6 1/2" components where the 4x10s go.  With the bass from the 10" sub of course.  That should produce a good 50/50 bass and treble combo.  I hate all those like  4 inch speaker and 5 15" JBL sub setups.  Lord only knows what they are singing, all you can hear is the BOOM BOOM BOOM.  Sounds like **** .  I will leave that to the ricers.   <P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||DaRkLoRD||08-05-2000||12:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>I hate all those like  4 inch speaker and 5 15" JBL sub setups.  Lord only knows what they are singing, all you can hear is the BOOM BOOM BOOM.  Sounds like **** .  I will leave that to the ricers.   <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>And me....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>I listen to trance music mostly now.. not much singing.. all synthesizers & drums. <P>I happen to like the BOOM BOOM BOOM.. hehe..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
